h of $y=f(5x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "To graph the function $y=f(5x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and compress it by factor of $5$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $5.$\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f8bd94b2652d96417690f4ddb67a3d6c3235dd828c98b9f0ddebf0cf2fb13c51.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115266 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "03cffed8-0c7f-5175-907c-3285cc07b2ec" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point that Lies on a Horizontally Stretched Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d73de5-7c0f-52cc-95b6-ac7d8905c7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529885} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4e075a-2c3d-5b91-ad1b-f0d083595868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-27,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530007} {:answer/id #uuid "caea27c1-ce8b-55b3-9c98-8e1c2d4fe10e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530089} {:answer/id #uuid "e549a086-100d-5f15-8002-3a18e0fcd22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530154} {:answer/id #uuid "e9772aa5-0fc4-50a4-b4da-335660752240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caea27c1-ce8b-55b3-9c98-8e1c2d4fe10e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530089} :answer-field/id #uuid "256febee-d392-5d02-9fce-d60999ce9e89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "218ab2ee-b004-5ca6-a364-899b69265503" :question/math-academy-id "q-79435" :question/problem "The point $P$ with coordinates $(-9,6)$ lies on the curve $y=f(\\frac{1}{3}x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)=f(3\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}x)),$ the function $y=f(x)$ represents a compression of the function $y=f(\\frac{1}{3}x)$ by a factor of $3$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(\\frac{1}{3}x)$ by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-9,6)$ on $f(\\frac{1}{3}x)$ is mapped to the point $(\\frac{(-9)}{3},6)=(-3,6),$ and this point must lie on the graph of $y=f(x).$"}]}
